skills/orchestration/herdr/SKILL.md

This file is a derivative work of SKILL.md from the Herdr project:

    https://github.com/ogulcancelik/herdr
    Copyright the Herdr authors
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0

Changes made to the original:

  - Added "Never target yourself" — excluding $HERDR_PANE_ID from fan-out
    target lists.
  - Added "Collect results through files, not the screen" — promotes the
    original's alt-screen fallback to the default result channel for work
    whose output will be acted on, with rules for per-worker paths, empty-file
    handling, and staleness.
  - Added "Coordinate a fleet" — multi-worker roster management, bounding
    worker count and timeouts, failure reporting, and when to prefer
    in-process subagents over a Herdr fleet.
  - Added "Handle a blocked worker" — permission posture at spawn, escalating
    approval prompts to the user rather than answering them, and not
    re-prompting a blocked agent.
  - Added "Tear down what you created" — closing only self-created panes.
  - Added "Trust boundary" — the socket's user-account-wide authority and
    treating worker output as untrusted data rather than instructions.
  - Extended "Safety and coordination rules" with the self-targeting rule.
  - Updated the frontmatter description to cover fleet coordination while
    keeping the original's conservative activation conditions.

The original sections on CLI discovery, layout primitives, IDs and caller
context, agent lifecycle and coordination, running commands in panes, and
read sources are retained substantially as written upstream.
